>> title: Phở Broth, Instant Pot
>> category: Soups
>> tags: beef, vietnamese, stock, star anise, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot pho broth, pressure cooker pho, pho broth in the instant pot, nuoc dung pho, pho stock, quick pho broth, weeknight pho
>> servings: 8
>> dish: pho-broth
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: pho-bo
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — under a locked lid you cannot skim, so the parboil and the scrub are the only chance it gets to come out clean
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot, a skillet for the spices, a fine sieve, the spice sachet
>> keeps: 4 days — the spices keep working in the fridge, so it is more aromatic on the second day, not less

>> step: parboil 10 min, rinse every bone
Cover @beef marrow bones{3%lb}(1.35 kg) and @oxtail{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) with @cold water{3%qt}(2.8 L) in the #Instant Pot{}, bring to a hard boil on Sauté and ~parboil{10%min}. Tip it into the sink, rinse every bone and scrub the inner pot.

>> step: char on Sauté 10 min
Char @yellow onions{2%large}(halved) and @fresh ginger{4%in}(halved lengthways) cut side down on the dry inner pot on Sauté ~char{10%min}, until blackened in patches. Lift them out and scrape the ash away.

>> step: toast 3 min, tie the sachet
Toast @star anise{5%whole}, @cinnamon stick{1}, @whole cloves{4}, @coriander seed{1%Tbs} and @black cardamom{1%pod}(cracked) in a dry #skillet{} ~toast{3%min}, until they smell like the shop, then tie them into a #spice sachet{}.

>> step: cook at high pressure 60 min
Lock @&(~3)parboiled bones{}, @&(~2)charred aromatics{} and @&(~1)spice sachet{} into the pot with @beef brisket{1 1/2%lb}(680 g) and @water{3%qt}(2.8 L), and ~pressure cook{60%min} at high pressure. In a six-quart pot, halve everything.

>> step: wait out the natural release 30 min, lift the brisket, pull the sachet
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{30%min}, then lift the brisket out and chill it — that is the sliced meat in the bowl — and pull the sachet.

>> step: season and strain
Season @&(~1)broth{} with @fish sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @rock sugar{1%oz}(30 g) and @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, then strain it through a fine sieve.
